ype": "concept", "title": "Version control basics"}], "description": "Students learn to keep raw data, cleaned data, and analysis outputs separate and auditable."}, {"id": "af9ad58b-3973-4cef-b16a-cce8f3f8f5eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Software workflows", "children": [{"id": "e54a7a8b-ccca-42c7-bfcd-5bbe3efedaea", "type": "concept", "title": "Spreadsheets for small audits"}, {"id": "7acae572-fbea-459c-a6c0-6897ecb03ef2", "type": "concept", "title": "SPSS/JASP/jamovi for guided analysis"}, {"id": "4483135c-e159-491d-b4cc-641641bc8565", "type": "concept", "title": "R or Python notebooks for reproducibility"}], "description": "The course supports multiple tools while emphasizing repeatable logic over button-click memory."}, {"id": "8e49296a-7154-4b40-8f6d-c92dbc75fd3a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reproducible reporting", "children": [{"id": "e51d79bb-b2e0-42d3-804b-ba0b1f1c0904", "type": "concept", "title": "Scripted outputs"}, {"id": "68cc077e-d011-4a89-b93e-7acaf87ccd76", "type": "concept", "title": "Appendices and replication files"}, {"id": "c6d53090-77cd-46de-9e97-2dd29bcef6b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Documenting assumptions"}], "description": "Students learn to make tables and figures traceable to data and code."}]}, {"id": "5f9ef946-e2dd-4683-a915-922f5f59afe4", "type": "topic", "title": "Communicating Statistical Findings to Courts, Agencies, Communities, and Policymakers", "description": "Turning analysis into clear, honest tables, visuals, briefs, testimony, and presentations.", "children": [{"id": "fb386ab1-6f4a-45df-9e1e-8e8bc9eed569", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audience-centered communication", "children": [{"id": "a0e2d1bd-914a-4a6b-ad14-fd6ecad05c76", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy memos"}, {"id": "07652ce0-0130-471f-b7ee-955b4d72da98", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency dashboards"}, {"id": "9a813542-156a-4deb-aef3-2ae6e33b09a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Community briefs"}], "description": "Students learn that the same analysis must be framed differently for courts, agencies, communities, and policymakers."}, {"id": "58a97344-324c-426e-b7c1-8880c9af4343", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Plain-language uncertainty", "children": [{"id": "0f205eff-c1ca-442b-a22f-8a6cf87bcc5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidence intervals in prose"}, {"id": "ded5c627-88fc-438a-ba4b-00cd2e9581e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual uncertainty"}, {"id": "69a893b6-6815-486d-9f65-46e40d4a42b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding exaggerated claims"}], "description": "The goal is to explain uncertainty honestly without making findings seem useless."}, {"id": "b924185e-852f-4bed-b9cc-911b0d7038ff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical presentation", "children": [{"id": "5443443a-25ae-420b-b80d-1b4edbdc7184", "type": "concept", "title": "Limitations sections"}, {"id": "720185ba-8449-4deb-98b6-203959cd8f47", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible tables and figures"}, {"id": "f5fcecde-5ff0-4174-9aa7-7886c45694b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Respectful language about people and places"}], "description": "Students learn to preserve nuance while making findings usable."}]}, {"id": "f801ced7-3fa7-436e-a7bd-15eedd10a99d", "type": "topic", "title": "Integrated Criminal Justice Statistics Capstone: Data Brief, Policy Memo, and Presentation", "description": "A final applied project using real justice data to answer a policy or practice question.", "children": [{"id": "1bc9f2e2-6aa8-4b36-9368-895c7d03565c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project design", "children": [{"id": "d94adb26-5366-483f-a181-3aa35165b892", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem statement"}, {"id": "67b3395f-7c41-4295-8d2b-8a062dd8d346", "type": "concept", "title": "Dataset selection"}, {"id": "30bc4390-ea12-4324-97f9-f7f4ccec6d50", "type": "concept", "title": "Analysis plan"}], "description": "Students choose a question that can be answered with available justice data and ethical limits."}, {"id": "f0b7b7ca-7b8c-486b-b7e1-766f49729bf8", "ty